 "title": "Quarterly Life Update Emails",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator shares how he sends a quarterly update email to friends, former bosses, coworkers, and investors every 90 days. He explains the structure of these updates and how they help keep people informed and open new doors.",
 "key_points": [
  "Send a quarterly email update every 3 months to friends, former bosses, coworkers, and investors.",
  "Include a TL;DR section for people who do not want to read the entire email.",
  "Include career and professional updates.",
  "Include personal updates.",
  "Share failures and learnings.",
  "Include any asks that you might have.",
  "The practice originally started to hold the creator accountable when starting his first business, and he continued it to keep people he met along the way updated on his life."
 ],
 "content": "Every 3 months i send update emails to 83 people, quarterly email to friends, former bosses, co workers, or people that have invested in me with an email update about the last 90 days have went, so what's inside. 1. TL;DR, 2. career, 3. personal, 4. failures and learnings, 5. asks that I might have. And I did this so other people could also hold me accountable when I was starting my first business. That didn't really work out, but I never stopped. I just do this now to keep people I've met along the way updated in how my life is going. That has opened so many doors and expanded my service area for luck that I never thought was going to happen. Give it a try and send one out tonight. Instagram reel/post by Jared Seidel. Text / caption: Everyone should do this. It’s easy and it’s such a high leverage way to stay in touch with people. On screen: Q3 Friend/Investor Update email draft.",
